# Database

Neon Postgres. `DATABASE_URL` in `.env.local` is production—the same database used by [techxiv.dev](https://www.techxiv.dev). There is no local database.

Schema: `prisma/schema.prisma`. Client: `src/generated/prisma`. App code uses `getPrisma()` from `src/lib/prisma.ts`.

## One-off queries and writes

Use the `db` script before writing one-off Prisma code:

```bash
npm run db -- recent [limit]
npm run db -- find <url-or-title>
npm run db -- virality <url-or-title> <score>
```

- `recent` returns the newest posts by `publishedAt`; the default limit is 1 and the maximum is 100.
- `find` canonicalizes a full URL for exact matching. Otherwise it searches title and URL case-insensitively, newest first, with a maximum of 20 results.
- `virality` requires exactly one match and writes an integer score from 0–100.
- Quote titles or URLs containing shell-sensitive characters: `npm run db -- find "multi-word title"`.

Output is JSON and includes post identity, classification, virality fields, and organization.

If the script cannot perform a needed operation, extend `scripts/db.ts` with a narrow command instead of creating disposable Prisma snippets. Treat all writes as production changes.

## Read-only fallback

If `DATABASE_URL` is unavailable, `GET https://www.techxiv.dev/api/posts` returns the recent public feed from the same database. It supports `cursor`, `orgs`, and `viral=1`; it does not support text search or writes.

Never print `DATABASE_URL` or other secrets.
